id: staggering-attack
name: Staggering Attack
kind: signature
side: advantages
tpCost: 6
requirement: N/A
description: >
  Your attack disrupts your opponent's balance, making it difficult for them to move.
text: >
  If you inflict Damage to an Opponent with this Attacking Maneuver, make a Might Clash
  against your Opponent. If you win, they gain the Staggered Combat Condition until the end
  of their turn.

---

# No script, for Knockback's reason: what it does is open a Clash, and a Clash is a card
# between two characters rather than a value on one of them.
#
# Opened the moment the Damage is taken off, which is where "if you inflict Damage" is
# first answered - and not off an Absolute Attack's miss, which is not Damage inflicted
# with an Attacking Maneuver for anything that triggers off it. Every Opponent it Damages
# has a Clash of their own.
#
# "Make a Might Clash" - not "you may", as Knockback's is. The card is opened either way;
# nothing is rolled until both sides say so, which is how every Clash here works.
#
# Winning it puts Staggered on them "until the end of THEIR turn", so the clock is theirs:
# the turn named is the target's, and nobody else's turn ending takes it off.
#
# Elemental (Plantlife) grants it for free, the way Launching grants Knockback.
